+# Cache Eviction Policy
+
+The project's current recorded decision is that the cache layer uses LRU (Least Recently Used) eviction, with cache entries configured with a 300-second time-to-live (TTL). LRU was chosen because it only tracks recency of access, which makes cache behavior simpler to reason about and more predictable.
